# Anvil Scanner Configuration
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment variable reference for anvil-scanner.
#
# Set these in your shell profile (~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc) or systemd unit:
#   export CLAUDE_KEY="your_key_here"
#
# Or copy this file to .env for local development:
#   cp config.example.env .env && chmod 600 .env
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── AI Provider Configuration ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default: Ollama (free, local, no account needed)
# Ollama must be running: https://ollama.ai
# Pull a model first: ollama pull llama3
#
# To use a cloud provider instead, set AI_PROVIDER and the matching key:
#   AI_PROVIDER=claude  → set CLAUDE_KEY below
#   AI_PROVIDER=openai  → set OPENAI_KEY below
#   AI_PROVIDER=grok    → set GROK_KEY below
#
# If AI_PROVIDER is not set, auto-detects in this order: Ollama (local probe) → CLAUDE_KEY → OPENAI_KEY → GROK_KEY.

# AI_PROVIDER=ollama          # ollama (default) | claude | openai | grok
# OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# AI_MODEL=llama3             # override model (llama3, mistral, gpt-4o-mini, claude-sonnet-4-6, grok-3-mini, etc.)

# Anthropic API key (only needed if AI_PROVIDER=claude)
# CLAUDE_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here

# OpenAI API key (only needed if AI_PROVIDER=openai)
# OPENAI_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here

# xAI Grok API key (only needed if AI_PROVIDER=grok)
# GROK_KEY=your_xai_api_key_here
# XAI_API_URL=https://api.x.ai/v1  # optional override

# ── Threat Intelligence ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AbuseIPDB API key (optional — enriches threat intel with abuse reports)
# ABUSEIPDB_KEY=your_abuseipdb_api_key_here
